<H1>Medium data</H1>
Search for medium no. = [1181].
<HR>
Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121&#176;C for 15 min.
<HR>
<P><B><FONT SIZE=3>1181&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;MODIFIED CELLULOLYTIC HALOARCHAEA MEDIUM</FONT></B></P>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> MDS salt water (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=574">574</a>)                 </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;833.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trace element solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1079">1079</a>)          </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Yeast extract (BD-Difco)                                </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Add components and bring volume to 958 ml with distilled water.   For preparation of solid medium, add 20 g/L agar (if necessary, use washed agar: see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=574">574</a>).  Autoclave.  After cooling, add the following solutions (autoclaved or *filter-sterilized) to the medium.  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 1 M NH<sub>4</sub>Cl                                            </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Potassium phosphate buffer (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=574">574</a>)       </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trace vitamins* (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=197">197</a>)                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 0.2 M Cellobiose solution </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;30.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Readjust pH to 7.0 with a sterilized 10% Na<sub>2</sub>CO<sub>3</sub> solution, if necessary.       <br>
